The only genuine nutritional concern in plant-based diets (B12) is easily addressed with a $5/month supplement — this applies to omnivores too, as B12 absorption declines with age regardless of diet.
Plant proteins, while sometimes lower in individual amino acids than meat, come bundled with fibre, phytochemicals, and vitamins that meat does not contain — the nutrient package is superior.
Populations eating traditional plant-based diets (rural Japan, India, Mexico) have dramatically lower rates of heart disease, obesity, and diabetes than those adopting Western meat-heavy diets.
